  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Capacities of Civil Society in Caraga and BARMM for Good Governance</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;In line with EU&#xbf;s mandate to support Civil Society in the Philippines, the proposed action will work with Civil society organizations (CSO) and CSO Networks in Caraga and Bangsamoro Autonomous Region of Muslim Mindanao (BARMM) regions to strengthen their role in public decision making at the local, regional and national level through tailored technical assistance, joint initiatives with LGUs and access to financial support. &lt;span style=&quot;color: black;&quot;&gt;The design of the action is the result of a detailed needs assessment conducted by PIN and the partners amongst CSOs working with marginalized groups, regional CSO networks, LGUs and community members in&lt;/span&gt; March-July 2021 with a follow up in March 2022. Over 90% of the respondents have &lt;strong&gt;highlighted the need to not only address the systemic barriers to CSO development, but also to increase coordination and level of dialogue between CSOs and LGUs. &lt;/strong&gt;Such an approach will result in better representation of the most socially and economically marginalized in the regions (women, youth, people with disabilities, indigenous people, internally displaced, and people living in conflict and disaster-prone areas) via CSOs having a stronger voice in policy. While CSOs across the Philippines are experiencing many challenges, those operating in Mindanao, particularly in the Caraga region and BARMM are often classified based on their political ideologies and religious orientation, therefore enjoy varying degree of access, acceptance and participation within the government structures and communities they operate in.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: yellow;&quot;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;To respond to these needs and the challenging enabling environment in which CSOs operate, &lt;strong&gt;People in Need (PIN), together with Maranao People Development Center Inc.&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;strong&gt;MARADECA) &lt;/strong&gt;and&lt;strong&gt; Balay Mindanaw Foundation Inc (BMFI) &lt;/strong&gt;designed a 24-month comprehensive action that will target 30 local and community CSOs, 4 CSO Networks and 30 LGUs at Barangay/Municipal level. Leveraging MARADECA and BMFI&#xbf;s combined 40 years of experience as peacebuilding experts and leaders in their communities, the following provinces have been identified as particularly relevant to the objectives of the action:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li data-list=&quot;bullet&quot; class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;ql-ui&quot; contenteditable=&quot;false&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BARMM&lt;/strong&gt;: Maguindanao (including Cotabato City), Special Geographic Areas/SGA (in North Cotabato), Lanao del Sur (including Marawi City) Basilan, Sulu and Tawi-tawi.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li data-list=&quot;bullet&quot; class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;ql-ui&quot; contenteditable=&quot;false&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Caraga&lt;/strong&gt;- Surigao del Sur, Agusan del Sur, Agusan del Norte and Surigao del Norte (including Surigao City).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
